From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 06:35:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] editor: slope view ring rule (kind 2,
 OCCUPY_CheckEdgeFlatness)

Structures with Physics.FlattenSkirt = true (nearly every building) are checked by
the engine with the 1-cell ring around the skirt against a pivot of ceil(last
sample), not with the area rule. EdOverlaySlope.h gets kind 2 "ring": CellRating
(a transliteration of the engine's loops), RateTile via sliding extremes on the four
ring bands (exact, in height words: float arithmetic on words is exact), Store::Invalidate
dirties the cell after a changed sample for this kind. ed_overlay_slope / ed_slope_at
accept 'ring' (KindFromName), ed_overlay_slope_caps() lists the kinds for a Lua
feature probe. Tests: ring rating equals the float transliteration of the engine on
random terrains for every skirt 1..16, the tile version equals the reference, store
invalidation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F37er45a7etRuMgEW1q3kY

